  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 8 - Arithmetic Operator
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_arithmetic_operators
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Arithmetic Operators
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: "Arithmetic Operators are symbols used to perform calculations on
    values.\n\nCommon arithmetic operators:\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>+</color></font>
    \u2192 addition\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>-</color></font>
    \u2192 subtraction\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>*</color></font>
    \u2192 multiplication\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>/</color></font>
    \u2192 division\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>%</color></font>
    \u2192 modulo (remainder)\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>//</color></font>
    \u2192 floor division\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>**</color></font>
    \u2192 exponent\n\nParentheses can be used to control calculation order:\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>(</color> <color=#7FDFFF>10</color> <color=#7FDFFF>+</color>
    <color=#7FDFFF>8</color> <color=#7FDFFF>)</color> <color=#7FDFFF>*</color> <color=#7FDFFF>2</color></font>\nThis
    ensures the addition happens first.\n\nExample:\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>a</color>
    = (<color=#7FDFFF>10</color> <color=#7FDFFF>+</color> <color=#7FDFFF>8</color>)
    <color=#7FDFFF>*</color> <color=#7FDFFF>2</color></font>\nResult: <color=#7FDFFF>36</color>\n\nThe
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>+</color></font> operator can also
    combine text (string values).\nExample:\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#FF6EC7>\"Hello
    \"</color> <color=#7FDFFF>+</color> <color=#FF6EC7>\"Robot\"</color></font>"
  isImageBig: 0
